<%#
  THE INDEX OF FILES (the Shop manual spec §9; the `project-organized` screen's last section): every
  file of the project, A TO Z as an index reads, each with the figure number it carries on this page
  — what the column's find box filters as you type and jumps from (figure_find_controller.js).

  ALWAYS THE PAGE'S LAST SECTION, AND NOT A PANEL OF THE LAYOUT. It holds no rows of its own — it is
  an index of what the panels above draw, the contents column's companion for files — so there is
  nothing for "+ Add panel" to open and nothing for the maker to arrange: projects/show draws it
  after every panel group, full width, numbered as the last section, whenever the page numbers a
  figure (ProjectsController#show's @index_rows). Not in the layout, so the editor, the visitor's
  page, its feed, its bundle and its BOM CSV are untouched (design-system.md rule 14).

  A FILE NO PANEL DRAWS IS LISTED WITH NO NUMBER — a browsed folder's, a nested repository's, a
  hidden panel's, the README the README panel renders — so the index stays an index of the project
  and its numbers stay ones the page can show. A stack's members each carry the stack's number.

  A LARGE PROJECT STAYS USABLE: the listing is already capped (Maker::ProjectFolderListing::FILE_CAP,
  and the note below says so), and the index shows the first SHOWN of what it holds with "Show all"
  for the rest. The find box searches every entry, the hidden ones included.

  A name that two files share says which folder each is in, as the screen's
  "harbor-number-v4.svg (project folder)" does; every entry's folder and kind ride on it for the find
  box and in its title. The name opens the file's page; the number goes to the figure.
%>
<% shown = ProjectsHelper::FILES_INDEX_SHOWN %>
<% names = @index_rows.map { |row| row.node.name.downcase }.tally %>
<section class="panel files-index" id="project-index" data-controller="files-index">
  <div class="panel-head">
    <h2>Index of files</h2>
    <%= section_note("index", @index_rows.size, "#{pluralize(@index_rows.size, 'file')}, A to Z, with each one’s figure") %>
  </div>
  <ol class="files-index-list">
    <% @index_rows.each_with_index do |row, i| %>
      <% number = figure_number(row.node_id) %>
      <% folder = row.section.presence || "project folder" %>
      <% kind = Maker::FileAttachment::ROLE_LABELS.fetch(row.role, "Other") %>
      <%= tag.li class: "files-index-entry", hidden: i >= shown,
                 data: { files_index_target: "entry", name: row.node.name.downcase, folder: folder.downcase, kind: kind.downcase,
                         entry_fig: number, beyond: (i >= shown || nil) }.compact do %>
        <%= link_to file_path(row.node_id), class: "files-index-name", title: "#{row.node.name} · #{folder} · #{kind}",
                    data: file_open_data do %><%= row.node.name %><% if names[row.node.name.downcase] > 1 %> <span class="files-index-folder muted">(<%= folder %>)</span><% end %><% end %>
        <span class="files-index-leader" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <% if number %>
          <%= link_to number, "#project-index", class: "files-index-fig", data: { fig_jump: number, action: "files-index#jump" },
                      "aria-label": "Fig. #{number}, go to the figure" %>
        <% else %>
          <span class="files-index-fig files-index-fig--none" title="No panel draws this file">—</span>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </ol>
  <p class="files-index-empty muted" hidden data-files-index-target="empty">No file matches.</p>
  <% if @index_rows.size > shown %>
    <button type="button" class="linkbtn files-index-more" data-files-index-target="more" data-action="files-index#showAll">Show all <%= pluralize(@index_rows.size, "file") %></button>
  <% end %>
  <% if @listing.truncated? %>
    <p class="muted files-index-truncated">
      The index lists the files this page lists, not every file in the folder.
      <%= link_to "Open the folder", files_path(folder: @listing.folder_id) %>
    </p>
  <% end %>
</section>
